		{
			"id": "evqr8fhRKsJI2fwIE",
			"description": "Bolt Pistol, Mk II Phobos-Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Phobos-pattern bolt pistol is a common Astartes sidearm, its grip and slide machined to mag-lock against a suit of power armour's thigh or chest plate when holstered. Codex background across many Chapters shows it as the Techmarine-serviced companion to the chainsword for close-quarters work once a boltgun's magazine runs dry.\n\nDesign: Same .75-calibre round and therefore the same damage line (5dx2(2) pi++ / 5d cr ex follow-up) as the Godwyn-De'az pattern above; only the frame differs. ST is raised to 12† to reflect the more robust, Astartes-proportioned grip: a Space Marine (ST 18-20 per the framework's Astartes physiology target) uses it one-handed with no penalty, while an unaugmented human struggles even two-handed. LC0 because, per the framework's legality table, Astartes-marked wargear is heresy for the unauthorised to possess even though the ammunition and mechanism are identical to a human-issue bolt pistol.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
