		{
			"id": "ekSS6Rcz6z5S5nL-l",
			"description": "Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Godwyn-De'az pattern is the boltgun the fiction treats as the baseline: a self-contained, rocket-assisted .75-calibre round whose motor ignites a few metres clear of the muzzle, widely depicted (Horus Heresy and modern Black Library alike) as capable of blowing an unarmoured man apart and reliably punching through carapace plate, while a Space Marine can shrug off a few hits from another Marine's boltgun before going down. Special Issue Ammunition (Kraken, Hellfire, Metal Storm, Vengeance) is Deathwatch's own term and rulebook material; Inferno bolts are that line's Deathwatch-specific incendiary load; sanctified/blessed ammunition is a recurring detail in Adepta Sororitas and Chaplain background with no stated mechanical difference against armour.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed boltgun anchor: 6dx2(2) pi++ with a 6d cr ex follow-up (per the framework's damage table; user-set minimum). Against Astartes power armour (torso DR 100) the armour divisor (2) drops effective DR to 50; 6dx2 averages 42, so it penetrates about 14% of hits (exact dice distribution) and still has to beat the wearer's HP with the pi++ wounding bonus and the 6d cr ex follow-up when it does, matching \"a Marine takes several bolts to kill another Marine.\" Against carapace (DR 45, effective DR 22) it penetrates 99% of hits, against Adepta Sororitas armour (DR 70, effective DR 35) 79%, and against an unarmoured man or flak (DR 12, effective DR 6) it is always lethal - all as the framework specifies. Against Mk X Gravis (DR 130, effective DR 65) it drops to 0.2%, and it essentially never beats a Terminator (DR 200, effective DR 100). Kraken keeps the same 6dx2 dice but swaps the armour divisor to (3) and drops the wounding modifier from pi++ to pi (less internal fragmentation, more punch) and shrinks the follow-up from 6d to 2d cr ex; against Astartes (effective DR 33) that raises penetration to 100%, and against a Terminator (effective DR 66) to 85%, trading wounding multiplier and blast for a much better chance of getting through heavy plate at all. Hellfire and Metal Storm are built from Deathwatch's stated design intent (anti-organic, anti-horde) translated into GURPS damage types (tox for the bio-payload, a fragmentation bracket for the flechette cloud) rather than lifted from any catalogue entry: Hellfire keeps the standard round's x2(2) mechanism but halves the dice (3dx2(2) pi, since most of the penetrator mass is sacrificed for payload) and its tox follow-up (3d(5) tox, organic targets only) is untouched by the rescale since it never interacted with DR the same way; Metal Storm is bumped from 5d pi [2d pi] to 7d pi [3d pi] to stay comfortably ahead of the new, higher flak/carapace baseline while remaining exactly what it was - a no-armour-divisor flechette cloud, lethal to unarmoured hordes and irrelevant against real plate. Vengeance and sanctified rounds are modelled as unchanged ballistically from the standard round (6dx2(2) pi++ / 6d cr ex), since neither RPG nor Codex material describes a different penetrator, with their special property left as a notes-level rule the GM applies. Inferno bolts keep the standard penetrator (6dx2(2) pi++) and double their incendiary follow-up from 4d to 8d burn ex, matching the doubled standard follow-up.",
