		{
			"id": "e04iv4uFM7RpyaR6k",
			"description": "Boltgun, Mk IV Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A simplified, mass-production pattern associated in Imperial Armour-style background with wartime attrition manufacture: cheaper to produce in bulk than Godwyn or Umbra lines, at some cost to finish and long-term reliability that the fiction gestures at without quantifying.\n\nDesign: Same anchor damage (6dx2(2) pi++, follow-up 6d cr ex); the only numeric difference from Godwyn is a lower cost (cheaper mass manufacture) and slightly lower weight. This project does not model a reliability penalty for it (no Malf value is given anywhere in this file), since the fiction never quantifies one; a GM wanting to dramatise \"mass-production and less reliable\" can assign a house Malf rating without touching these numbers.",
