		{
			"id": "e88TUlcwXp_B9owzP",
			"description": "Storm Bolter",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Twinned boltgun barrels sharing a single trigger and (usually) a large drum or box magazine, standard wargear for Terminator squads and a common pintle/hull weapon on Imperial vehicles; Codex and Horus Heresy background consistently shows it as simply \"two boltguns fired together,\" not a more powerful round.\n\nDesign: Same .75-calibre bolt and therefore the same damage line (6dx2(2) pi++ / 6d cr ex follow-up, identical to the standard Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern's penetration checks) as the Godwyn anchor; \"rof: 3x2\" captures the twin-linked barrels doubling the effective volume of fire per the standard GURPS convention for linked weapons, and the 60-round magazine matches the larger drums shown in art and background. Listed here for infantry (Terminator, ST 12) use with Guns (Rifle); a vehicle- or turret-mounted storm bolter should instead use Gunner (Machine Gun) per the framework's skill table, with no change to the damage line.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
